/// json parse and stringify.
///
/// `parse` turns a json string into candela values: an object becomes a map
/// keyed by strings, an array becomes a list, and a scalar becomes an int,
/// float, string, bool, or null. The result is typed `any`, so read a field
/// back with a downcast (`v as int`, `v as {string: any}`) or a type test
/// (`v is int`). A malformed string raises a catchable error.
///
/// `stringify` serializes any candela value back to a json string.
///
/// This module is pure Candela over the runtime's own json primitives, so it
/// compiles into a `.cdlb` artifact that runs under `candela-vm` with no
/// dynamic library.

/// Parses a json string into a value (typed `any`).
fn parse(text) {
    return json_parse(text);
}

/// Serializes a value to a json string.
fn stringify(value) {
    return json_stringify(value);
}
